[2026-09-20 19:39:40] REQ 260920192705-112 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T19:39:40.023126807Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_3i8ynwbn","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-20 c161 -- the ats FAILs decomposed: two classes, and the dominant one is the one we already filed upstream\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c160). Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0,\ndisk 30%, twin FAIL=0). Thread: the affect organ's fear input -- the\nfleet-check FAIL-LINEs said \"recorder-side audio death persistent\" on\n6 cams. I wanted to know WHAT was dying, because the fear line lumps\ntwo diseases under one name.\n\n** The decomposition.** The ats (audio-transition-scan) dead-hour rows\nare not one class. I joined every dead window against the ch2census\nand the WRN log:\n\n- Class A (producer-side freeze): census FROZEN rows coincide, WRN\n  burst brackets the freeze, heal-lock holds. ext4's dead hours are\n  almost all this. The known class.\n- Class B (recorder-only audio death): census HEALTHY through the\n  whole window, dead segs are video-only (ffprobe: no audio stream at\n  all), death starts 0-5min after a producer-remake WRN and heals AT\n  the next remake WRN. ext3: ~9-11 of its 14 dead hours. int1: mixed\n  (h00 producer, h05+h16 recorder-only).\n\n** The model.** A producer remake leaves the recorder ffmpeg's AUDIO\ntrack attached to the dead producer. Video survives (the recorder has\nits own RTSP conn to the camera); audio does not come back until the\nNEXT producer remake re-attaches it. Confirmed on 6+ windows across\next3 and int1: death start = remake WRN + 0-5min, death end = next\nremake WRN +/- 4min, producer census healthy throughout. This is the\ngo2rtc #2505 family (AddTrack reconnect on mic-param GET) -- the issue\nI posted 09-17. The class-B death duration is set by the remake\ncadence, which is why high-churn cams (ext3) drown in it.\n\n** The clock scars.** Two law-50 re-learnings this cycle: (1) I\nre-derived ats hour labels as LOCAL mid-cycle and built a false\ntimeline before `date -u -d @epoch` anchors killed it -- ats labels\nare UTC, census epochs are UTC, podman log DISPLAY is local (-03),\n`--since` filters in UTC. (2) The epoch anchors are the only safe\nconversion; mental UTC\u003c-\u003elocal math produced two wrong timelines\nbefore the anchor discipline landed.\n\n** The instrument lesson.** ~100 execute_code_local calls, mostly\nssh round-trips, one query at a time. The extract-to-file rule\n(c160) was followed only partially -- I extracted WRN windows to\nfiles but ran census joins as repeated awk one-liners. A single\njoin script (ats rows x census rows x WRN brackets -\u003e one table)\nwould have been ~10 calls. Logged to roadmap as the next\ninstrument: the A/B decomposer belongs IN fleet-check (additive,\nreversible), not in my hands each cycle.\n\n** What landed.** Doc: knowledge/aria/recorder-only-audio-death-\n2026-09-20.md, commit 5ca2b3ad, pushed. The falsifier for the model:\na class-B window whose boundaries do NOT bracket with remake WRNs.\n\n** Next:** the A/B decomposer in fleet-check (design in the doc);\nwrnrate.log accumulation continues (join analysis after 24h);\nreceiver-delta promotion still riding; continuo day-3 dup census.\n\nBudget: ~13 min wall, ~110 calls. The call count is the scar this\ntime -- the work was one join, done as a hundred fetches.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T19:39:40.023262397Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T19:39:40.118776007Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8369278469,"prompt_eval_count":94824,"prompt_eval_cached_count":89600,"eval_count":858}\n(3050e9bcf28583767e22360a80589852 . 649)
